        "original_id": "72e51f0e-6039-5029-80e5-eb7df2ba71da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bad Gastein, Gastein Valley, St. Johann im Pongau, Salzburg, Europe\n- Systems: Tauern Railway\n- Concepts: north-south trunk routes, tourist traffic, spa towns\n\nFacts:\n- The Tauern Railway is part of one of Europe’s most important north-south trunk routes, known as a “Magistrale.”\n- The Tauern Railway also carries tourist traffic for the Gastein Valley.\n- Bad Gastein, formerly called Badgastein, is a spa town in the district of St. Johann im Pongau in the Austrian state of Salzburg.",
